 Linux + Bash Scripting (Intermediate Level)

 Focus: Production Linux + Automation

🔹 Linux Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• Difference between soft link and hard link (with real use case)
• Explain Linux boot process
• What happens when a Linux system runs out of memory?
• Zombie vs orphan process
• How do you find which process is using high CPU or memory?
• How do you troubleshoot a slow Linux server?
• How does top, htop, vmstat, iostat help in production?
• How do you check open ports and active connections?
• Explain file permissions with real scenarios
• What is ulimit and why is it important?
• How do you manage log rotation?
• How do you secure a Linux server?

🔹 Bash Scripting (Intermediate)

• Difference between #!/bin/bash and #!/bin/sh
• How do you pass arguments to a shell script?
• $@ vs $*
• Exit codes and error handling
• How do you write reusable bash scripts?
• Functions in bash
• set -e, set -x, set -o pipefail
• How do you schedule scripts using cron?
• Bash script for monitoring disk usage
• Bash script for application health check
• Bash vs Python — when to use which?

💡 Interview Tip (2–4 yrs):
Always add real examples like:
👉 “I used a bash script to monitor disk usage and trigger alerts in production.”

